  "published": "2026-10-29T09:37:20.673Z",
  "releaseNotes": "﻿### Fixed\n- Formatter glob patterns without a directory prefix (e.g. \"Foo*.cs\") are matched against the current directory correctly instead of being mis-sliced by its length, which previously caused no-match or wrong-file results\n- Generated dependabot npm section now emits a valid directory value (e.g. \"/\") for a root-level package.json instead of an empty string, and normalizes directory separators to forward slashes, so GitHub no longer rejects the generated dependabot.yml\n- Tracking hash generator no longer includes generated obj/bin/.git files, so no-change detection works reliably\n### Changed\n- Replaced em dash characters with plain punctuation across this repository's own documentation, code comments, tests, and label definitions, so generated text no longer contains them\n- The never-close label description now uses a semicolon instead of an em dash; managed repositories pick up the new description on their next update-template run\n- Resynced the label descriptions in docs/github-labels.md to match the generated labels\n- Dependencies - Updated Nullable.Extended.Analyzer to 1.17.1\n- Dependencies - Updated FunFair.BuildCheck to 474.2.21.2862\n- SDK - Updated DotNet SDK to 10.0.403\n- Dependencies - Updated Meziantou.Analyzer to 3.0.317",
